  dbg_pause.pcpp - Debugger compliance: pause

  Pausing a running program: an endless loop with no breakpoint at all.
  The REPL holds a program with no breakpoint at its entry until c; the
  editor runs it at F5. A pause stops it wherever it is.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    REPL:   pcpp res\tests\dbg_pause.pcpp -d   then type each step's words
    Editor: open res\tests\dbg_pause.pcpp, F5, then each step's keys
  Each step: what to type, then "->" what both front-ends show.
  Pause: REPL Ctrl+C, editor F6 (or the Pause button).

  Keys (REPL word = editor key):
    c = F5 (continue)   n = F10 (over)   s = F11 (into)
    finish = Shift+F11 (out)   q = Shift+F5 (stop)
    b N = click the gutter left of line N
    bt = the CALL STACK   f N = click CALL STACK row N (0 = top)
    locals = the VARIABLES pane   p X = a WATCH row for X (hover is the same)
    the program's output and keyboard = the console the REPL runs in /
    the editor's TERMINAL tab

  Steps:
   1. (start)          -> REPL: held at entry (no breakpoint);
                          editor: running, "spinning" in the TERMINAL tab
                          at once (not only when the program ends)
   2. c                -> REPL only: running, "spinning" printed at once
   3. pause            -> stops (pause) at 56 or 55
      p GCount         -> a count above 0
   4. c, pause         -> stops again, p GCount is larger
   5. q                -> the program is stopped
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dbg_pause;

var
  GCount: int64;

begin
  println("spinning");
  while true do
    GCount := GCount + 1;
  end;
end.
